From: Alexandr Mironov <7062352+alexandr-mironov@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] device-xiaomi-vayu: ship the panel driver in the initramfs

The DSI panel drivers for this device (`panel-huaxing-nt36672`,
`panel-tianma-nt36672`) are built as modules, and the device package does not
list them anywhere, so they never end up in the initramfs.

Anything that has to draw on the screen before the rootfs is mounted therefore
has no display: the plymouth boot splash stays dark, and — more importantly —
full disk encryption is unusable, because the passphrase prompt (plymouth plus
buffyboard as the on-screen keyboard) renders into nothing. The device is not
bricked in that state, since postmarketOS brings up USB networking in the
initramfs and the volume can be unlocked over SSH, but a phone that needs a
computer on every boot is not a phone.

Use the per-kernel `modules-initfs.$kernel` mechanism of devicepkg-dev so each
panel variant pulls in only its own driver.

Tested on Xiaomi POCO X3 Pro (vayu_global, M2102J20SG) with the Huaxing panel:
`/usr/lib/modules/initramfs.load` now contains `panel_huaxing_nt36672` and the
module is present inside the generated initramfs.

